Description

The dataset I plan to use contains information on individuals’ demographic, lifestyle, and
regional attributes and their corresponding medical insurance charges. Key variables include
age, sex, BMI, number of children, smoking status, region, and Cost. This dataset provides
explores how different personal habits and demographics influence healthcare costs. My main
hypothesis is that smokers and individuals with higher BMI values will have significantly higher
insurance charges. I also want to explore whether there are any regional disparities in
healthcare expenses.
